  "verbalization": "Rufinamide appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving participation in sodium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Rufinamide binds to multiple sodium channel subunits—Scn11a, Scn4a, and Scn2a—each of which participates in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This activity is then linked to Scn8a, indicating a potential role for Rufinamide in modulating sodium channel function in Scn8a. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with the shared involvement of voltage-gated sodium channel activity as a critical intermediary step. The mechanism appears to be driven by the binding of Rufinamide to different subunits, which in turn influence the activity of Scn8a. While the exact functional significance of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated, the integrated evidence points to a plausible pathway where Rufinamide modulates sodium channel activity in Scn8a through a common mechanism involving voltage-gated sodium channels.",
